{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRJWLTENREF65Tg1fAeF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WifC3fSTd8dMF55dR6F9WK","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-fKOPbS/memory/utc-only-date-methods.md","content":"---\nname: utc-only-date-methods\ndescription: Repo rule: date code must use only UTC Date methods (Date.UTC, getUTCDate, getUTCMonth, etc.), never local-time ones\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nDate code in this repository uses only the UTC methods: `Date.UTC`, `getUTCDate`, `getUTCMonth`, `setUTCMonth`, `getUTCFullYear`, etc. Never use the local-time ones: `getDate`, `getMonth`, `setMonth`, `new Date(year, month, day)`.\n\n**Why:** Invoice dates are stored as midnight UTC, but the servers run in America/Los_Angeles. Local-time methods therefore shifted dates by a day. This caused a bug where invoices created just after midnight got a due date one day off (found the week before 2026-11-26).\n\n**How to apply:** When writing or reviewing any date logic (due dates, month arithmetic, date construction), use the UTC variants. Flag any local-time Date method you find in the code.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":369,"cache_read_input_tokens":21709,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":369,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6ddacae-a1cd-4f1a-baa0-71823753aa4d","uuid":"4298aa50-a3ea-4aed-b0d6-eb9a3cc5da5c","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:28:13.816Z","request_id":"req_011ChRJWLB7TnLCn2dNMtaFr","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01WifC3fSTd8dMF